  "id": "Compound::DB01192 - Gene::4985",
  "verbalization": "Oxymorphone is linked to Oprd1 through a series of molecular and pharmacological pathways that collectively highlight its role as an opioid agonist. The evidence suggests that Oxymorphone, as an opioid agonist, binds to the opioid receptor family, which includes Oprd1, and is part of a broader class of full opioid agonists. This is supported by the fact that Oxymorphone is included in the Full Opioid Agonists category, which also encompasses Levorphanol and Hydromorphone, all of which bind to Oprd1. The lowest common ancestors of these entities—Opioid Receptor Agonist and Morphinane Alkaloid—underscore the shared pharmacological profile of these compounds. The integration of these pathways indicates that Oxymorphone exerts its effects by activating Oprd1 through a mechanism that involves binding to the receptor, thereby contributing to the broader opioid action. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Oxymorphone and Oprd1, mediated through the opioid receptor agonist class, and highlights the role of morphinane alkaloids in this process.",
